OL,3,GNEWSAGas worker says he was told to lie
OL,4,Aby supervisor
OL,5,
OL,6,FWright was heard telling police
OL,7,FArmstrong, who was his supervisor,
OL,8,Fasked him to lie if anyone asked if
OL,9,Fthey had done a test and he said could
OL,10,Fnot "go against" what Armstrong asked
OL,11,Fof him.
OL,13,FBoth gas workers and Lee Ward deny 10
OL,14,Fcounts of gross negligence
OL,15,Fmanslaughter. Island Energy also pleads
OL,16,Fnot guilty to a combined health and
OL,17,Fsafety case.
